- op: create  # 4273
  at: '2026-05-28T18:29:55Z'  # 4273
  by: agent  # 4273
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4273
  clock: 1  # 4273
  nonce: '4273'  # 4273
  data:  # 4273
    kind: invariant  # 4273
    title: "verify-claims silently confirms must_not_exist on empty source dir (security FP)"  # 4273
    status: violated  # 4273
    priority: 0  # 4273
    parent:  # 4273
    tags:  # 4273
    - dogfooding  # 4273
    - pass9  # 4273
    - security  # 4273
    - verify_claims  # 4273
    isbefore: []  # 4273
    duplicate_of: []  # 4273
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 4273
    pr_ref:  # 4273
    description: "Repro: mkdir /tmp/empty && cd /tmp/empty && cat >claim.yml <<EOF\nclaims: [{id: c1, text: 'No file writes', constraint: {boundary: fs_write, must_not_exist: true}}]\nEOF\nhypergumbo verify-claims --claims claim.yml --json   # confirmed, exit 0.\n\nSecurity impact: CI runs verify-claims from a wrong cwd (build artifact dir, misconfigured pipeline) -> all security claims silently pass. Suggested fix: require behavior_map node count > N before any confirmed verdict; otherwise emit error/warning. Found in dogfooding pass 9 (2026-05-28)."  # 4273
    fields:  # 4273
      statement: "When verify-claims is invoked without --input from a directory containing no analyzable source files, every must_not_exist claim returns 'confirmed' with evidence_count=0 and exit 0, instead of producing an error or warning about the empty analysis."  # 4273
      root_cause: "No guard checks that the auto-discovered/auto-run behavior_map contains a non-trivial node count before honoring 'no chains found -> confirmed' verdicts. The fail-silent path matches the empty-truth fallacy already documented for taint-* (II) and unknown constraint type (AA)."  # 4273
- op: discuss  # 7fa5
  at: '2026-05-28T20:06:24Z'  # 7fa5
  by: agent  # 7fa5
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7fa5
  clock: 2  # 7fa5
  nonce: 7fa5  # 7fa5
  message: "pass11: new schema manifestation. Claims with 'constraint' dict lacking must_not_exist=true/max_chains/taint_flow are silently confirmed as 'No constraint to check'. Boundary-centric schema (only must_not_exist=true|max_chains|taint_flow are recognized) silently no-ops any other constraint shape. Users writing structurally similar but unrecognized schemas (e.g., must_exist: kind: function) get false 'confirmed' verdicts with zero warning."  # 7fa5
